<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="33449" href="schedule/2012/fall/CWL/220/33449.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2012" href="schedule/2012.xml">2012</calendarYear><term id="120128" href="schedule/2012/fall.xml">Fall 2012</term><subject id="CWL" href="schedule/2012/fall/CWL.xml">Comparative and World Literature</subject><course id="220" href="schedule/2012/fall/CWL/220.xml">Origins of Western Literature</course></parents><sectionNumber>A  </sectionNumber><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: Nightmares of Nero This course provides an in depth study of the culture and literature of Rome in the 50s and 60s CE. Special emphasis will be placed on the works of Seneca, Petronius, and Lucan. In particular, the course will ask how and in what ways their gruesome and maddening texts reflect life in the Neronian age.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2012-08-27Z</startDate><endDate>2012-12-12Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>11:00 AM</start><end>11:50 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MWF    </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>1065</roomNumber><buildingName>Lincoln Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Traill" firstName="A">Traill, A</instructor><instructor lastName="Walters" firstName="B">Walters, B</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>